    "원자료 R03428의 적용 맥락: Using the ESEE firm-level panel for Spanish manufacturing (1990–2006, ~1,800 firms across 20 two-digit NACE industries), this paper studies which domestic firms are acquired by foreign parents (foreign ownership ≥50%) and how acquisition affects innovation (product/process, foreign-technology assimilation), exports and productivity. The unit is the firm; identification leverages within-firm variation over time, industry and year controls, and propensity-score reweighting to address time-varying selection in the Spanish manufacturing/multinational entry context."
